{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/245083-best-additions-to-the-core-rules","id":245083,"title":"Best additions to the core rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-30T17:52:40-07:00","id":245083,"title":"Best additions to the core rules?","content":"By the time I received my Demon Core, there have been five and a half supplements released for the line. Each one is filled to the brim with lovely setting material and clever mechanics, but there are a few bits of setting and rules from each that really make the gameline's rules shine for me.<br /> <br /> <b>Heirs to Hell</b>: The whole book was amazing, but demon-blooded cipher was what really clinched it for me. No one else has such a dread destiny to avoid as the demons' children.<br /> <b>Flowers of Hell</b>: The chapter on subverting infrastructure was invaluable. (New gadget rules are pretty awesome as well.)<br /> <b>Interface</b>: So many amazing little toys in this book, but the rules for conditional pacts and the pact market are the final touch that really match the mechanics to the setting presented in the core.<br /> <b>Splintered City Seattle</b>: The Apocalypse Vault is the stuff of Supernatural season finales.<br /> <b>Ready Made Characters</b>: Sample Interlocks and Ciphers. Invaluable.<br /> <b>Mortal Remains</b>: Technically a hunter book, but it still shouldn't be missed, at the least for its new mortal antagonist &quot;The Knights of Saint Adrian.&quot; Bail bondsmen for the Angels.<br /> <br /> I've been unfair for just picking one thing from each book. What are your favorites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T19:22:41-07:00","id":245134,"title":"","content":"Electromagnetic Linguistics from <b>Flowers of Hell</b> is very cool and pretty clever. I jumped for it for my Demon character with grabby hands.<br /> <br /> Galatea from <b>Splintered City: Seattle</b> offers interesting insight into one potential angle on the nature of the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> My favorite supplement addition to Demon: the Descent, from the books you name, is the lesser demons, and specifically imperatives, in <b>Mortal Remains.</b> Of <i>course</i> it's not just the angels that are important and powerful enough to be self-aware that Fall. A lot can be done with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T17:38:14-07:00","id":245729,"title":"","content":"I've got give credit to Splintered City: Seattle. Not only is it packed with great ideas for a Demon game, but I hope it sets a precedent for future City books to follow. From the the descriptions of the city, to the adventure seeds, the NPCs (Stray WILL find a way into my game someway/somehow!), and how they cover how all the other Supernaturals interact with the city. I absolutely love this book and I just want the writers to know how great I think their work was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/284-mason","name":"Mason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T18:01:37-07:00","id":245738,"title":"","content":"I think the book is lucky in that the Demon: The Descent core covers basic Seattle details like locations and stuff really well, facilitating Splintered City's structure nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T20:25:30-07:00","id":245834,"title":"","content":"Are they going to be available for those that missed the Kickstarter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T06:15:58-07:00","id":246108,"title":"","content":"Yes, the pattern is for Kickstarter backers to receive the stretch goal supplements first, give time for them to do an editing pass, and then release the corrected PDF to backers and put it up for general sale. <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/131284/Heirs-to-Hell\" target=\"_blank\">Heirs to Hell</a> and the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/127589/ReadyMade-Player-Characters-Demon-the-Descent\" target=\"_blank\">Ready-Made Characters</a> are already available for general purchase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T09:09:07-07:00","id":246182,"title":"","content":"As it should be! I'm happy to wait. Next time I'll be in at the ground floor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}